target/
**/*.rs.bk
_to_delete/

# The benchmark's durable sink and its private copy of the rendered document.
#
# The segment is a *working file*: `bench --run` opens it under `SyncPolicy::Always`, writes
# every durable append of every run into it, and the bytes differ on every run by
# construction. Tracking it meant a benchmark could not be run without dirtying the tree,
# which is the same defect as writing the committed results document without `--publish`,
# one file over. The CSVs — the raw results the table is rendered from — stay tracked.
results/E16-wallclock/nilestream-bench.seg
results/E16-wallclock/nilestream-report.seg
results/E16-wallclock/E16-wallclock.md
results/E23-scaling/E23-scaling.md

# Python bytecode caches. `thesis/include-results.py` is run by `make reproduce`, and its
# cache was tracked for several cycles: 22,935 bytes carrying the absolute path of the
# machine that built it, in a repository whose whole argument is that what is committed can
# be accounted for.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
